  <metadata>
    <name>Bourbon Heritage: the family distillers of the Rolling Fork country</name>
    <desc>Out from Bardstown into the Nelson, Washington and Marion county hollows: the Willett farm, Henry McKenna&apos;s Fairfield, Jacob Beam&apos;s Hardin&apos;s Creek and a Beam descendant&apos;s distillery at Lebanon. Public, exact waypoints only. Private land and approximate stops are omitted. https://kyhistorydrive.com/drives/bourbon-heritage/</desc>
    <link href="https://kyhistorydrive.com/drives/bourbon-heritage/"><text>Bourbon Heritage: the family distillers of the Rolling Fork country</text></link>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="37.7855" lon="-85.4618">
    <name>1. Willett Distillery</name>
    <desc>Visiting: Working distillery; tours by reservation, fees apply. Paid admission, Reservation needed</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="37.5819" lon="-85.2718">
    <name>4. Limestone Branch Distillery (Lebanon)</name>
    <desc>Visiting: Working distillery; tours by reservation, fees apply. Paid admission, Reservation needed</desc>
  </wpt>
